1) Additional /backup/ service, 
which gathers fx rates, currently using only 1, 
and if for some reason it is down, the app will not work, because
it relies on it for rates.



This is our concurrency strategy

# Idempotency strategy is using Pessimistic row locking.

It means that when a conversion starts, the service will later execute the following:
balanceRepository.findAllByClientIdForUpdate(client.getId());

The database will lock that client's balance rows until the transaction finishes.


Therefore
cannot accidentally be spent twice by two simultaneous transactions.

This is particularly suitable for this assignment because it gives us a simple and very clear transactional guarantee.



2) GET /conversions?transactionId=…&date=YYYY-MM-DD&clientId=…&page=…&size=… →
paginated history filtered by transactionId, date, or clientId (at least one filter must be
provided).


